  "description": "Native approximate FP32 SFU instructions in register recurrence loops; primary result is signed board-power contrast vs the same bounded remap loop without the SFU instruction. Not isolated SFU rail energy. No global/shared/local access in the hot loop; one 4-byte sink store per logical lane after the loop. Q and chain sweeps assess sustained throughput; native TANH is explicitly unavailable on V100.",
